`pkgs.formats.hocon` uses **pyhocon** to validate generated HOCON, but pyhocon does not implement `classpath` includes. Therefore, classpath includes can fail validation even if the HOCON is intended for a Java/Scala HOCON parser.

Use either:

```nix
format = pkgs.formats.hocon {
  doCheck = false;
};
```

or provide an alternative validator via the `validator` option. The documentation explicitly recommends one of these approaches for classpath includes.

Additionally, a nixpkgs issue reports that the `type = "classpath"` generator itself appears broken and that the validator fails to parse its output.  
Sources: [HOCON format documentation](https://docharvest.github.io/docs/nixos/development/settings-options.section/), [nixpkgs issue #329448](https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/issues/329448)
